# AIDA distributed store (orphan branch worktree)
# Pattern matches both the directory (in the canonical worktree) and a
# symlink (in `aida session start`-created sibling worktrees, which
# point back at the canonical store). Without the bare-name pattern,
# git treats the symlink as a tracked file. trace:EPIC-21 | ai:claude
.aida-store/
.aida-store

# AIDA runtime state — deny-by-default. Anything under .aida/ is per-clone
# runtime state (cache, sessions, roles, env shims, review prompts, server
# data, etc.) unless explicitly allow-listed below. Adding a new runtime
# file under .aida/ requires no gitignore change; tracking a new
# project-config file requires adding an explicit `!.aida/<name>` line.
# trace:BUG-73 | ai:claude
.aida/*

# Tracked exceptions: project-level config that lives in the repo.
!.aida/config.toml
# AIDA-using discipline guides are checked in with the project. trace:STORY-829 | ai:codex
!.aida/discipline/
!.aida/discipline/**
# Project-level command aliases are shareable across the team. trace:TASK-877
!.aida/aliases.toml
!.aida/reserved-paths.toml
!.aida/docker-compose.yml
!.aida/docker-compose.dev.yml
!.aida/setup.sh
.antigravitycli/
docs/writeups/

# SPIKE-31: per-clone derived rules generated by `aida rules sync` from
# the spec graph. Regenerated on demand; would thrash across worktrees if
# committed. Hand-authored rules outside this subdir remain tracked.
.claude/rules/aida-specs/

# TASK-625: per-machine runtime locks from Claude Code's /schedule + /loop
# scheduler (e.g. `.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock`) — never source. (`*.yaml.lock`
# is covered separately; no tracked `.claude/*.lock` exists.) trace:TASK-625
.claude/*.lock

# TASK-383: planning-pass drafts — scratch plans written by a loop of
# `/aida-plan` over queue items; promote to docs/plans/<name>.md when adopted.
# Gitignored so they don't linger untracked and abort a later PR's pull. trace:TASK-383
docs/plans/_draft/

# Rendered/shareable artifacts live in joemooney/artifacts, not the code repo.
*.pdf

# Legacy pre-git-canonical store snapshots (live store is the orphan aida-store branch)
requirements*.yaml
scaffold-report.html

# mdBook rendered output (derived artifact)
docs/cli/book/

# The AIDA Book rendered output (derived)
docs/book/

# mdbook-mermaid vendored lib (2.6MB — regenerate via `mdbook-mermaid install docs`)
docs/mermaid.min.js
__pycache__/

# ── Personal dotfiles at the repository root ────────────────────────────────
# This repository is PUBLIC. These are the filenames that accumulate
# machine-local and employer context over time — a proxy setting, an internal
# host, a work email in .gitconfig, a corporate alias in a shell rc. None of
# them has ever been committed here, and the point of this block is to keep it
# that way: without it, one `git add -A` by a human tidying a dirty tree, a
# broad add by an agent, or a scaffolding step publishes whatever has since
# filled them.
#
# Named entries rather than a root glob, so the rule states what it protects
# against and a genuinely new project dotfile still has to be decided on
# rather than silently swallowed. Same deny-by-default intent as the .aida/
# block above. trace:BUG-1511 | ai:claude
/.bashrc
/.bash_profile
/.bash_login
/.profile
/.zshrc
/.zprofile
/.zshenv
/.gitconfig
/.ripgreprc
/.inputrc
/.netrc
/.npmrc

# Codex agent config (BUG-1511 criterion 2, decided rather than left open):
# `.codex/hooks.json` wires local hooks with ABSOLUTE machine paths, so it is
# per-machine state. `.codex/config.toml` is portable project configuration —
# three lines registering the aida MCP server, the Codex twin of the tracked
# `.mcp.json` — so it stays trackable and is deliberately NOT ignored here.
# `.codex/skills/` is a scaffolded pack like `.claude/skills/` and is left
# trackable for the same reason. trace:BUG-1511 | ai:claude
/.codex/hooks.json

# `.codex/hooks/` — the ten handler scripts the wiring above points at — is
# IGNORED too, decided rather than left open. It is NOT tracked even though
# `.claude/hooks/` carries the same ten script names, because the two are not
# the same kind of object. `.claude/hooks/` is tracked as ten SYMLINKS into
# `aida-core/templates/hooks/`, so those script bodies are in git exactly once
# at their master, and its manifest (`.claude/settings.json`) is itself tracked
# and uses portable `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR` paths. The Codex side is generated
# output: `scaffold_codex_hooks` WRITES COPIES of those same embedded masters,
# so tracking them would add a second copy of already-tracked content — the
# per-vendor forking that module's own header says the design exists to
# prevent. And it would buy a fresh clone nothing: the only file that wires
# these handlers is `.codex/hooks.json`, ignored just above, so the scaffolder
# has to run regardless — and that one pass writes the handlers and the wiring
# together. Untracked-and-unignored is the one state that is neither.
# trace:BUG-1511 | ai:claude
/.codex/hooks/
